  "chapter": 238,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 11 Chapter 238\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 6353-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  in  relation  to permitting the use of municipal space for\n        outdoor dining; and providing for the repeal of such  provisions\n        upon the expiration thereof\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill codifies authorization provided by Executive Order to allow\nrestaurants to operate outdoors on municipal sidewalks and streets. This\nauthorization provided a much-needed lifeline for restaurants during the\nCOVID-19 public health emergency, when outdoor dining presented a  pref-\nerable  option,  or  the only option, for customers with reduced risk of\nCOVID-19 transmission.\n \n  Continuation of this program will build on other supports provided  by\nthe  State to allow impacted restaurants to build back better, including\nthe  $800  million  COVID-19  Pandemic  Small  Business  Recovery  Grant\nProgram.\n \n  I  have  secured  an agreement with the Legislature to include several\namendments ensuring the bill can be successfully and safely implemented.\nSince the outdoor space authorization was  first  granted  by  Executive\nOrder,  municipalities  have been critical partners in ensuring space is\navailable and can be safely utilized. The amendments to the  bill  allow\nthe  existing  approval  process  used  by the SLA and municipalities to\ncontinue, and maintains the jurisdiction for  code  enforcement  on  the\nlocal  municipality  to  ensure any structures or space used is safe for\nuse. On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
